cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  orrery-lab: an interactive 3D solar system built on real celestial mechanics
message: >-
  If you use this software or its figures, please cite it. The underlying
  catalogues have their own citation requirements — see `references` below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Ramon
    alias: DanielRamon10
repository-code: "https://github.com/DanielRamon10/orrery-lab"
url: "https://danielramon10.github.io/orrery-lab/"
abstract: >-
  A computational orrery. Planetary positions are solved from published
  Keplerian elements rather than looked up, and everything built on top —
  a browser 3D scene, N-body integrators, statistical tests, two machine
  learning models and a Gaia star field — rests on that same physics.
  Includes measured comparisons of symplectic against non-symplectic
  integration, a stability dataset generated by simulation rather than
  downloaded, and worked demonstrations of target leakage and Malmquist
  bias.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - celestial-mechanics
  - orbital-mechanics
  - n-body-simulation
  - symplectic-integrators
  - exoplanets
  - gaia
  - scientific-computing
  - data-visualization
license: MIT

references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Keplerian Elements for Approximate Positions of the Major Planets
    authors:
      - family-names: Standish
        given-names: E. M.
    institution:
      name: Jet Propulsion Laboratory, Solar System Dynamics Group
    url: "https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/approx_pos.html"
    notes: Source of the orbital element table in orrery/elements.py.

  - type: article
    title: "Dynamics of systems of two close planets"
    authors:
      - family-names: Gladman
        given-names: Brett
    journal: Icarus
    volume: 106
    start: 247
    year: 1993
    doi: 10.1006/icar.1993.1169
    notes: >-
      Source of the analytic Hill-stability criterion used as the baseline
      in orrery/models.py.

  - type: database
    title: NASA Exoplanet Archive
    institution:
      name: NASA Exoplanet Science Institute, Caltech/IPAC
    url: "https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/"
    notes: >-
      Confirmed planet catalogue and the Kepler Objects of Interest table.

  - type: database
    title: Gaia Data Release 3
    institution:
      name: European Space Agency, Gaia Data Processing and Analysis Consortium
    url: "https://www.cosmos.esa.int/web/gaia/dr3"
    notes: >-
      Stellar positions, parallaxes and photometry. Funding for the DPAC is
      provided by national institutions participating in the Gaia
      Multilateral Agreement.
